(Plan 291 required verification: a multi-branch `append ... but if ... but
if ... otherwise append ...` chain, mirroring the existing multi-branch
print test (018_fizzbuzz.vox has three `but if` branches). Confirms the
continuation loop in the shared chain-builder (comma/but/and) still works
for `append`, not just `print`.)

a buffer called b15 is 64 bytes in size.
a number called n15 is 15.
Append "x" to b15, but if n15 modulo 15 is equal to 0 append "fizzbuzz", but if n15 modulo 3 is equal to 0 append "fizz", but if n15 modulo 5 is equal to 0 append "buzz".
Print b15.

